---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Projects & Experience - Pavel Kleisner">

    <section class="page-head">
        <div>
            <h1>Quest log</h1>
            <p class="sub">Long-lived platforms, production integrations and a few tools of my own. Client systems are private, so here is what I owned on each, which constraints mattered and what the work taught me.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="book">
        <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
            <p>Quest log</p>
            <a href="#client">Main and side quests</a>
            <a href="#own">Own projects</a>
            <a href="#before">Before DataLite</a>
        </nav>

        <div>
            <section class="chapter" id="client">
                <h2>Main and side quests</h2>
                <p class="sub">All through a long-term collaboration with DataLite since 2017, first as an employee, for the last several years as an independent contractor.</p>
                <div class="quests">
                    <article class="quest">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-main">Main quest</span><h3>TSM / CETIN</h3><span class="when">2020 – now</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Senior backend and integration engineer, team lead</p>
                        <div class="quest-body split">
                            <p>Backend and integration work on a modern service management platform for a telco operator. I work close to production, on releases, B2B communication with partners, process rules and data compatibility.</p>
                            <ul class="objectives">
                                <li>Lead the production rollouts of 2.2 and 2.4</li>
                                <li>Core developer on version 1.5</li>
                                <li>Integration flows: ticketing, NIP, change management, B2B, PEW</li>
                                <li>Incident analysis from logs, metrics and data</li>
                                <li>Planning, explaining and code review as the main developer for our part of the platform</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <p class="stack"><b>Stack:</b> Kotlin, Java, Spring, PostgreSQL, Kafka, Kubernetes</p>
                    </article>

                    <article class="quest">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-side">Side quest</span><h3>Nordic web</h3><span class="when">2024 – now, on demand</span></div>
                        <div class="quest-body split">
                            <p>Ad-hoc collaboration on a Django-based web system. The volume is low these days, but the engagement stays open and I jump in when there is a focused change to make.</p>
                            <ul class="objectives">
                                <li>Self-service and web behaviour in Python, Django and templates</li>
                                <li>Targeted changes without forcing my usual patterns onto the codebase</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <p class="stack"><b>Stack:</b> Python, Django, templates</p>
                    </article>

                    <article class="quest">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-done">Completed</span><h3>MNCP</h3><span class="when">2018 – 2021</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Full-stack engineer</p>
                        <div class="quest-body split">
                            <p>Measurement, archives, exports and operational workflows. This is where I moved from delivering features to owning behaviour across backend, frontend and database.</p>
                            <ul class="objectives">
                                <li>Authentication, export fixes, archive filters and measurement batches</li>
                                <li>Database scripts and deployment alongside the application code</li>
                                <li>Following a bug through the whole request and data flow</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <p class="stack"><b>Stack:</b> Kotlin, Spring, Angular, Oracle, PostgreSQL</p>
                    </article>

                    <article class="quest">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-done">Completed</span><h3>ZIS</h3><span class="when">2017 – 2018</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Enterprise Java</p>
                        <div class="quest-body split">
                            <p>An enterprise application for CETIN operations: Java and ZK screens, controller, service and DAO layers, imports, Excel processing and production defects.</p>
                            <ul class="objectives">
                                <li>Complete business screens from the UI down to persistence</li>
                                <li>A classic enterprise stack with strict process and data rules</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <p class="stack"><b>Stack:</b> Java, ZK, ZUL, Maven, SQL</p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="own">
                <h2>Own projects</h2>
                <p class="sub">Smaller things I build and run myself, mostly together with AI agents. They keep me close to the whole loop: an idea, a usable interface, data, deployment and maintenance.</p>
                <div class="side">
                    <article>
                        <h3>Parcel pickup map</h3>
                        <p>Every parcel pickup point and box in the Czech Republic on one map, around 40,000 of them, imported daily from carrier feeds and deduplicated.</p>
                        <p class="stack"><b>Next.js, PostgreSQL, Drizzle, Leaflet</b></p>
                    </article>
                    <article>
                        <h3>Family portal</h3>
                        <p>Self-hosted apps on a small home server: meal plans with real nutrition data, a planner for everything around the house, trips and packing lists.</p>
                        <p class="stack"><b>Next.js, Drizzle ORM, PostgreSQL, Raspberry Pi</b></p>
                    </article>
                    <article>
                        <h3>Trading bot</h3>
                        <p>A trend-following strategy (EMA crossover, ATR stop) for testing assumptions against market data, not for selling certainty.</p>
                        <p class="stack"><b>Python, Freqtrade</b></p>
                    </article>
                    <article>
                        <h3>This website</h3>
                        <p>Static, bilingual, cheap to run and easy to change. The <a href="https://github.com/JohnyIII/pavelkleisner.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">source is on GitHub</a>.</p>
                        <p class="stack"><b>Astro, TypeScript, Cloudflare Pages</b></p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="before">
                <h2>Before DataLite</h2>
                <p>Software tester at GMC Software (now Quadient) in Hradec Králové, 2013–2014: use cases, test scenarios and running the team's Jenkins server.</p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="party">
        <div>
            <h2>Want to talk about a project?</h2>
            <p>Long-term or focused contracts, remotely from near Prague.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:contact@pavelkleisner.dev">contact@pavelkleisner.dev</a>
    </section>

</Layout>
